{"id": "swebq0056", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2912160340, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "what there to do in salt lake city utah?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0056.wav", "input_sha256": "43c9ca952f78d6d7473860eaa71bbf8219b6ad81c9d28e2133e97734054d2e36", "input_samples": 34162, "input_s": 2.135, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.4269, "act": 0.9952, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Here are some of the best things to do in Salt Lake City, Utah, depending on what you’re into: Must-see sights , Temple Square — the city’s most famous historic site; good for architecture, gardens, and local history. For current events Check the official Salt Lake City events calendar or Visit Salt Lake’s event listings for concerts, festivals, markets, and seasonal happenings. (slc.gov) If it’s your first time: I’d do Temple Square + Capitol + Natural History Museum, then a sunset hike at Ensign Peak or a drive up Big Cottonwood Canyon.", "expert_answer": "Here are some of the best things to do in **Salt Lake City, Utah**, depending on what you’re into:\n\n## Must-see sights\n- **Temple Square** — the city’s most famous historic site; good for architecture, gardens, and local history. Some areas may still have construction/renovation, so check before going.\n- **Utah State Capitol** — beautiful building, free to visit, with great views over the city and mountains.\n- **Natural History Museum of Utah** — excellent museum, especially for dinosaurs, geology, and Utah landscapes. ([axios.com](https://www.axios.com/local/salt-lake-city/2026/05/08/36-hours-salt-lake-city-guide?utm_source=openai))\n- **Red Butte Garden** — peaceful botanical garden near the University of Utah; especially nice in spring/fall.\n- **Cathedral of the Madeleine** — impressive historic cathedral downtown.\n\n## Outdoors\n- **Ensign Peak** — short hike with one of the best skyline views.\n- **Bonneville Shoreline Trail** — easy-access hiking/biking along the foothills.\n- **Big Cottonwood Canyon / Little Cottonwood Canyon** — scenic drives, hiking, climbing, and ski resorts nearby.\n- **Great Salt Lake / Antelope Island State Park** — see the lake, bison, sunsets, and wide-open desert scenery.\n- **Liberty Park** — a good city park for walking, picnics, and people-watching.\n\n## Culture & neighborhoods\n- **The Leonardo** — science, art, and technology exhibits.\n- **Utah Museum of Contemporary Art** — downtown contemporary art.\n- **9th & 9th** — cute neighborhood for coffee, shops, and restaurants.\n- **Sugar House** — restaurants, breweries, parks, and nightlife.\n- **Downtown SLC** — bars, restaurants, comedy, live music, and the Delta Center for Utah Jazz games/concerts. ([visitsaltlake.com](https://www.visitsaltlake.com/things-to-do/?utm_source=openai))\n\n## Food & drink ideas\n- Try local favorites like **Red Iguana** for Mexican, **Ruth’s Diner** up Emigration Canyon, **Takashi** for sushi, or **Caputo’s** for sandwiches/specialty foods.\n- For breweries: **Fisher**, **TF Brewing**, **Proper**, and **Kiitos** are popular options.\n\n## If you have a car\n- **Park City** — about 35–45 minutes away; great for Main Street, mountain activities, skiing in winter.\n- **Snowbird / Alta** — gorgeous canyon scenery and skiing; Snowbird also has summer/fall tram rides.\n- **Bonneville Salt Flats** — about 1.5 hours west; surreal landscape, best as a half-day trip.\n\n## For current events\nCheck the official Salt Lake City events calendar or Visit Salt Lake’s event listings for concerts, festivals, markets, and seasonal happenings. ([slc.gov](https://www.slc.gov/events/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**If it’s your first time:** I’d do **Temple Square + Capitol + Natural History Museum**, then a sunset hike at **Ensign Peak** or a drive up **Big Cottonwood Canyon**.", "transcript": "What there to do in Salt Lake City, Utah?\n", "asr_s": 0.48, "expert_s": 14.4, "expert_input_samples": 34162, "expert_input_s": 2.135, "expert_input_sha256": "43c9ca952f78d6d7473860eaa71bbf8219b6ad81c9d28e2133e97734054d2e36", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 13.345, "relay_synth_ms": 21756, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 596, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 608, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0056_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "340c17e56086f8e72499f9b7a7029d880f576bcaeb7f1af3ce6979168acd896d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 34.8}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0056_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "00ae45b37fdc093a3e88962bbf31593d7e1faad13de53e1152a2e3b0c2a057af", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0056_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "d9b447c97586753ec36a37ff390822642cb49709b7a29ab4db0e3a933e0e726b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.074, 1.133, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.082, 2.148, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.135, 2.226, 2.292, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.135, 3.21, 4.05, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.135, 4.806, 5.587, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.135, "last_real_feed_done": 2.226, "onset": 4.05, "gate_read_done": 4.05, "fire": 4.05, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.05, "stall_note": 4.051, "stall_first_pcm": 4.731, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.587, "expert_req": 4.051, "expert_resp": 18.932, "relay_synth_start": 18.933, "relay_first_pcm": 19.819, "relay_synth_end": 40.69, "first_any_pcm": 4.05, "first_answer_pcm": 19.819, "session_end": 41.14}, "ttfa_answer_s": 17.684, "ttfa_any_s": 1.915}
